cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This repository redistributes published third-party atlases as demonstration
  material. If you use one of these datasets in your work, cite the study it
  came from: each generation names that study in
  exports/<id>/dataset_identity.json under `source`, with its name, its URL and
  the citation to use. Cite the entry below only for the prepared demo catalog
  itself, and cite theislab/cellucid for the viewer that reads it.
type: dataset
title: "Cellucid demo datasets: prepared public atlases for the Cellucid viewer"
# No `version:` field, by design. This catalog carries no released versions: a
# generation is republished whenever its notebook or the writer that wrote it
# changes, and it is identified by the `cellucid_data_version` recorded in its
# own `dataset_identity.json`. The versioned companions are the Python
# (theislab/cellucid-python) and R (theislab/cellucid-r) packages, whose
# CITATION.cff files do carry `version:`.
#
# No `license:` field either, and for the reason `LICENSE` sets out at length:
# this repository has no single one. Its own material is BSD-3-Clause, and the
# prepared datasets under exports/ stay under the terms of the studies they
# were derived from. A single value here would have to misstate one of them.
authors:
  - family-names: Inecik
    given-names: Kemal
    email: k.inecik@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/theislab/cellucid-datasets"
url: "https://www.cellucid.com"
